commit afad92bf1b78e33c53b9018fef31233cefcb5225
Author:     Jeong, YunWon <69878+youknowone@users.noreply.github.com>
AuthorDate: Thu Sep 24 12:21:26 2026 +0900
Commit:     GitHub <noreply@github.com>
CommitDate: Thu Sep 24 12:21:26 2026 +0900

    Add OrderedDict, marshal, inspect, and chflags bitflagset (#8780)
    
    * Implement _collections.OrderedDict
    
    Extracted from #6799: native OrderedDict as a dict subclass,
    iterator mutation tracking, and mapping-view set operations.
    
    * Add OrderedDict, warnings source lines, and socket sendmsg
    
    Implement _collections.OrderedDict as a dict subclass with a
    linked list of insertion-order nodes.
    
    Pack struct F/D as native float/double complex pairs, and report
    unexpected __replace__ field names as a list repr.
    
    Register encodings.latin_1 at startup. Reject NUL in input()
    prompts. Copy non-exact type dicts in mapping order.
    
    Fetch warning source lines through _bless_my_loader and unicode
    splitlines. Keep the last warnings.filters list after deletion.
    
    Snapshot sendmsg sequences before converting buffers, parse
    ancillary ints with __index__, and dispatch AF_CAN by protocol.
    
    Store sys.trace and sys.profile on each ThreadSlot so
    _settraceallthreads/_setprofileallthreads are visible to
    sys.gettrace/getprofile on other threads.
    
    Use <frozen importlib._bootstrap> as frozen importlib
    co_filename. Keep HEAPTYPE socket objects GC-tracked.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Load marshal via readinto and dump sets in dumps order
    
    marshal.load fills a scratch buffer with readinto on a
    contiguous writable memoryview, and rejects a returned length
    other than the requested size.
    
    set and frozenset dumps write elements in sorted(v,
    key=marshal.dumps) order.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Add classmethod_descriptor and ABC IS_ABSTRACT flags
    
    Give METH_CLASS methods a distinct classmethod_descriptor type.
    Store Py_TPFLAGS_IS_ABSTRACT from __abstractmethods__ and look
    up that attribute only in the type's own dict.
    
    Expose defaultdict.default_factory as a member descriptor.
    Inherit bool's unused number slots from int. Mark set and
    frozenset __contains__ as METH_COEXIST.
    
    Parse classmethod, staticmethod, object.__new__, and heap type
    text signatures. Register interactive source in linecache.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * address review: odict reuse, descr call, new wrapper
    
    Reuse odict node slots and walk the live list in next_after.
    Require both | operands to be dicts. Drop the odict iterator
    on GC clear. Bind classmethod descriptors through descr_get
    and update IS_ABSTRACT under the type lock. Give odict keys
    and items sq_contains. Walk tp_new_wrapper past new_wrapper
    so HEAPTYPE socket subclasses can call socket.__new__.
    Split FreeBSD Bluetooth protocol constants from Linux values.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Represent chflags bits with bitflagset
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Represent access and mode bits with bitflagset
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Continue unfinished REPL suites as incomplete input
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Add pickle and os.stat inspect signatures
    
    Give _pickle.Pickler the clinic constructor text signature and
    accept fix_imports and buffer_callback as positional-or-keyword.
    Allow #[pyfunction(text_signature)] and use it so os.stat reports
    (path, *, dir_fd=None, follow_symlinks=True). Uncomment import
    _pickle and drop the pickle inspect expectedFailures.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Add Unpickler, dump/load, and lstat signatures
    
    Give _pickle Unpickler, dump, dumps, load, and loads clinic
    text signatures, and os.lstat (path, *, dir_fd=None).
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Complete OrderedDict with insertion-order links
    
    Move the native OrderedDict into ordered_dict.rs and track order
    with a linked list of nodes, keeping mapping-view set operations.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * address CI: stat casts, HCI_DATA_DIR, passing xfails
    
    Compare stat permission bits as Mode so Linux clippy does not
    flag a u32-to-u32 cast. Export HCI_DATA_DIR with the Bluetooth
    socket option values. Drop expectedFailure from tests that now
    pass.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Fix wasm teardown deadlock and bluetooth constants
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Clear process-wide eval breaker bits in STW test
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Drop exclusive-held panic that tripped wasm clippy
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Fix OrderedDict contains and export Windows BDADDR
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Add cmp_to_key and hash-once LRU cache
    
    _functools.cmp_to_key now returns KeyWrapper. LRU lookups store the
    key hash on _lru_list_elem so __hash__ is not called again on hits
    or eviction.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Allow subclass keywords on list, tuple, and float
    
    list.__init__ rejects keywords only when tp_new is still list's.
    tuple/float.__new__ reject them only when tp_init is still the base's.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Fix CI lint, test re-export, and structseq members
    
    Drop the duplicate clear_eval_breaker_for_test re-export.
    Format structseq imports. Expose struct sequence fields as
    readonly members so assignment raises "readonly attribute".
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Allow subclass keywords on itertools and filter
    
    Positional-only constructors ignore extra keywords when a subclass
    has replaced tp_init, matching list/tuple/float.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Remove text_signature derive parameter
    
    Drop the string override on #[pyfunction] and #[pyclass]. Signatures
    are generated from the Rust parameter list only. Restore inspect
    expectedFailures that depended on the override.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Rename set contains_method to __contains__
    
    Keep a borrowed contains helper for slots and C-API. The coexist
    pymethod is named __contains__.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Use MonitoringEvent instead of EVENT_* aliases
    
    Drop the unused MonitoringEvents bitflags and the EVENT_PY_START
    style mask constants. Call sites use the enum and .mask().
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Store warnings filters as PyListRef
    
    The list already serializes its elements. Drop the extra mutex around
    the cached list pointer.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Re-export clear_eval_breaker_for_test after rebase
    
    Keep the STW test helper visible without bringing back stop_bit_set.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Fix groupby reentrancy and islice arguments
    
    Give _grouper its own tgtkey and take currvalue after the key
    comparison. Accept __index__ on islice bounds, reject step 0, and
    drain the source up to stop.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * SETREF warnings filters, onceregistry, and defaultaction
    
    Keep the last list, dict, or str after the module attributes are
    deleted by swapping the interpreter cache pointer. Do not store a
    None fallback for _warnings_context.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Iterate OrderedDict inner dict via next_entry
    
    &PyDict is not an iterator after the borrowed-ref signature change.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Remove expectedFailure from testBluetoothConstants
    
    Linux now exports BTPROTO_HCI and the rest of the set.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Borrow get_filter arguments as PyObject
    
    Match the warn_explicit call site that passes borrowed
    handles after the internal-helper borrow change.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Fix bool slots and SemHandle safety docs
    
    Leave unused bool number slots unset so inspect reports
    __add__ on int. Document SemHandle::from_raw safety.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Keep sendmsg errors and drop duplicate linecache
    
    Replace sendmsg iterable TypeError only. Register REPL
    source in linecache once per compiled input.
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Nest REPL parse or-patterns for clippy
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    * Mark pydoc os.stat signature test expectedFailure
    
    Assisted-by: Grok:grok-4.6
    
    ---------
    
    Co-authored-by: Lee Dogeon <dev.moreal@gmail.com>

